{"authored" [{"question" "q-71268" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find a direction vector of the line that is given as the intersection of the planes $z=1$ and $x=y.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040648/state.json" "file_sha256" "316e47fbe9ef982da62b8c3e0919a1bca97ae1a218d29b4c152e2986ca3f89ef" "basis" 1464 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040648/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-71268" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, notice that: \n\n- For the plane $z=1$, a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨0,0,1⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $x=y$ (or $x-y=0$), a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨1,-1,0⟩.$\n\nTo find a direction vector for the line, we calculate the cross product of these normal vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & ={n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} \\\\  & =⟨0,0,1⟩\\times ⟨1,-1,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =i+j \\\\  & =⟨1,1,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040648/state.json" "file_sha256" "316e47fbe9ef982da62b8c3e0919a1bca97ae1a218d29b4c152e2986ca3f89ef" "basis" 1464 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040648/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-71268" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040648/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b175b0ab4ad058714b06a2abaf7cc561e52cfebf3ef81caada55893e769e68f2" "basis" 1464 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040648/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-71268" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040648/state.json" "file_sha256" "316e47fbe9ef982da62b8c3e0919a1bca97ae1a218d29b4c152e2986ca3f89ef" "basis" 1464 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040648/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-71268" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨-1,0,0⟩"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040648/state.json" "file_sha256" "316e47fbe9ef982da62b8c3e0919a1bca97ae1a218d29b4c152e2986ca3f89ef" "basis" 1464 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040648/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-71268" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨0,0,1⟩"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040648/state.json" "file_sha256" "316e47fbe9ef982da62b8c3e0919a1bca97ae1a218d29b4c152e2986ca3f89ef" "basis" 1464 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040648/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-71268" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨0,1,-1⟩"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040648/state.json" "file_sha256" "316e47fbe9ef982da62b8c3e0919a1bca97ae1a218d29b4c152e2986ca3f89ef" "basis" 1464 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040648/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-71268" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨1,-1,0⟩"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040648/state.json" "file_sha256" "316e47fbe9ef982da62b8c3e0919a1bca97ae1a218d29b4c152e2986ca3f89ef" "basis" 1464 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040648/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-71268" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨1,1,0⟩"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040648/state.json" "file_sha256" "316e47fbe9ef982da62b8c3e0919a1bca97ae1a218d29b4c152e2986ca3f89ef" "basis" 1464 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040648/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-129170" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find a direction vector of the line that is given as the intersection of the following two planes:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-3x+4z-11=0 \\\\ x-2y+31=0\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040648/state.json" "file_sha256" "316e47fbe9ef982da62b8c3e0919a1bca97ae1a218d29b4c152e2986ca3f89ef" "basis" 1464 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040648/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-129170" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we notice:\n\n- For the plane $-3x+4z-11=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨-3,0,4⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $x-2y+31=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨1,-2,0⟩.$\n\nTo find a direction vector for the line, we calculate the cross product of these normal vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & ={n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} \\\\  & =⟨-3,0,4⟩\\times ⟨1,-2,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -3 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =8i+4j+6k \\\\  & =⟨8,4,6⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040648/state.json" "file_sha256" "316e47fbe9ef982da62b8c3e0919a1bca97ae1a218d29b4c152e2986ca3f89ef" "basis" 1464 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040648/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-129170" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040648/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b175b0ab4ad058714b06a2abaf7cc561e52cfebf3ef81caada55893e769e68f2" "basis" 1464 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040648/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-129170" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040648/state.json" "file_sha256" "316e47fbe9ef982da62b8c3e0919a1bca97ae1a218d29b4c152e2986ca3f89ef" "basis" 1464 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040648/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-129170" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨4,0,3⟩"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-worker